From cdf27194cc21b4bb6f5d8cf92a1042b42889aab7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 23:40:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Give inputstream.ffmpegdirect the FFmpeg reconnect options

The options are added only when the inputstream is inputstream.ffmpeg or
the stream is HLS, so a channel played through inputstream.ffmpegdirect
gets none of them, although it hands exactly these options to FFmpeg:
GetFFMpegOptionsFromInput() accepts reconnect, reconnect_at_eof,
reconnect_streamed and reconnect_delay_max.

Without them a dropped connection ends the stream, and Kodi answers the
end of a live stream by playing the next item in the playlist, which on a
channel list is a different channel.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 src/iptvsimple/utilities/StreamUtils.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/iptvsimple/utilities/StreamUtils.cpp
+++ b/src/iptvsimple/utilities/StreamUtils.cpp
@@ -517,7 +517,8 @@ bool StreamUtils::ChannelSpecifiesInputs
 bool StreamUtils::SupportsFFmpegReconnect(const StreamType& streamType, const std::string& inputstreamName)
 {
   return streamType == StreamType::HLS ||
-         inputstreamName == PVR_STREAM_PROPERTY_VALUE_INPUTSTREAMFFMPEG;
+         inputstreamName == PVR_STREAM_PROPERTY_VALUE_INPUTSTREAMFFMPEG ||
+         inputstreamName == INPUTSTREAM_FFMPEGDIRECT;
 }
 
 std::string StreamUtils::GetUrlEncodedProtocolOptions(const std::string& protocolOptions)
